citeturn6search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 13.2 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Zhu et al. confirmed Conjecture 1.4 for outerplanar graphs in [26]. ... Otherwise, there is at least one component with at least five vertices. ... The equitable \\Delta -coloring conjecture holds for outerplanar graphs\n\nConjecture 1.1\n\nIf 𝐺 is a connected graph which is neither a complete graph nor odd cycle, then 𝜒𝑒⁡(𝐺) ≤𝛥⁡(𝐺).\n\nIn 1994, Chen et al. [4] put forth the following conjecture.\n\nConjecture 1.2\n\nFor any connected graph 𝐺, if it is different from a complete graph, a complete bipartite graph, and an odd cycle, then 𝜒∗𝑒⁡(𝐺) ≤𝛥⁡(𝐺).\n\nChen et al. [4], [3] proved Conjecture 1.2 for graphs with 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≤3 or 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥|𝑉⁡(𝐺)|2 or a tree. Yap and Zhang [22], [23] showed that Conjecture 1.2 holds for outer planar graphs and planar graphs with 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥13. Lih and Wu [14] verified that 𝜒∗𝑒⁡(𝐺) ≤𝛥⁡(𝐺) for bipartite graphs other than complete bipartite graphs. Wang et al. [20] proved Conjecture 1.2 for line graphs, and Kostochka et al. [9], [10], [11] proved it for graphs with low average degree, outerplanar graphs, and 𝑑-degenerate graphs with 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥14⁢𝑑 +1. Wu et al. [21] confirmed Conjecture 1.2 for planar graphs with large girth. Recently, Tan [18] confirmed Conjecture 1.2 when 𝐺 is a planar graph without 4-cycles and 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥7.\n\nFor a graph 𝐺 and a list assignment 𝐿 assigned to each vertex 𝑣 ∈𝑉⁡(𝐺) a set 𝐿⁡(𝑣) of acceptable colors, an 𝐿-coloring of 𝐺 is a proper vertex coloring such that for every 𝑣 ∈𝑉⁡(𝐺) the color on 𝑣 belongs to 𝐿⁡(𝑣). A list assignment 𝐿 for 𝐺 is 𝑘-uniform if |𝐿⁡(𝑣)| =𝑘 for all 𝑣 ∈𝑉⁡(𝐺). A graph 𝐺 is equitably 𝑘-choosable if, for any 𝑘-uniform list assignment 𝐿, 𝐺 is 𝐿-colorable and each color appears on at most ⌈|𝑉⁡(𝐺)|𝑘⌉ vertices.\n\nIn 2003, Kostochka, Pelsmajer, and West investigated the equitable list coloring of graphs. They proposed the following conjectures in [12].\n\nConjecture 1.3\n\nEvery graph 𝐺 is equitably 𝑘-choosable whenever 𝑘 >𝛥⁡(𝐺).\n\nConjecture 1.4\n\nIf 𝐺 is a connected graph with maximum degree at least 3, then 𝐺 is equitably 𝛥⁡(𝐺)-choosable, unless 𝐺 is a complete graph or is 𝐾𝑘,𝑘 for some odd 𝑘.\n\nIt has been proved that Conjecture 1.3 holds for graphs with 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≤3 in [16], [19]. Kostochka, Pelsmajer, and West proved that a graph 𝐺 is equitably 𝑘-choosable if either 𝐺 ≠𝐾𝑘+1,𝐾𝑘,𝑘 (with 𝑘 odd in 𝐾𝑘,𝑘) and 𝑘 ≥max⁡{𝛥,|𝑉⁡(𝐺)|2}, or 𝐺 is a connected interval graph and 𝑘 ≥𝛥⁡(𝐺) or 𝐺 is a 2-degenerate graph and 𝑘 ≥max⁡{𝛥⁡(𝐺),5} in [12]. Pelsmajer proved that every graph is equitably 𝑘-choosable for any 𝑘 ≥𝛥⁡(𝐺)⁢(𝛥⁡(𝐺)−1)2 +2 in [16]. Conjecture 1.2, Conjecture 1.4 were proved for planar graphs 𝐺 without 4- and 6-cycles and 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥6 by Li et al. in [13]. Zhu et al. confirmed Conjecture 1.2, Conjecture 1.4 for each planar graph 𝐺 without 3-cycles and 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥8, and for each planar graph 𝐺 without 4- and 5-cycles and 𝛥⁡(𝐺) ≥7 in [25]. Zhu et al. confirmed Conjecture 1.4 for outerplanar graphs in [26]. Zhang et al. proved Conjecture 1.2, Conjecture 1.4 for series–parallel graphs in [24]. More results can be seen in [5], [6].\n\nIn this paper, we improve the results in [13], [18], [25] and obtain that every planar graph 𝐺 is equitably 𝑘-choosable and equitably 𝑘-colorable if 𝐺 has no 4-cycles and 𝑘 ≥max⁡{𝛥⁡(𝐺),6}.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquitable Coloring of IC-Planar Graphs with Girth g ≥ 7 (https://www.mdpi.com/2075-1680/12/9/822)\nciteturn6search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.2 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; Kostochka [18] proved that Conjecture 2 holds for outerplanar graphs. ... In 2016, Zhang [26] first considered the equitable coloring of 1-planar graphs and obtained that Conjecture 2 holds when \\Delta \\ge 17, which was improved to \\Delta \\ge 15 by Zhang, Wang and Xu [27] in 2018. ... If the order of each component of G is at most five, then \\Delta \\le 4.\nChen and Lih [16], Lih and Wu [17] showed Conjecture 2 holds for